Sure! To create a new `ChartSeries` with your specified settings and attach it to a chart layout, you’ll need to supply the following:

| Parameter | Description |
|-----------|-------------|
| `labels` | An array of strings for the X‑axis labels (e.g., `["Jan", "Feb", "Mar"]`). |
| `data` | An array of numbers corresponding to each label (e.g., `[10, 15, 7]`). |
| `color` | A string specifying the default color for the series (e.g., `"blue"`). |
| `chartLayout` | The chart layout object where the series will be added. |

Here’s a quick example using placeholder values:

```javascript
const labels = ["Jan", "Feb", "Mar"];
const data = [10, 15, 7];
const color = "blue";
const chartLayout = { /* your chart layout object */ };

const newSeries = ChartSeriesGenerator({
    labels: JSON.stringify(labels),
    data: JSON.stringify(data),
    color: color,
    chartLayout: JSON.stringify(chartLayout)
});
```

